# Fetched and derived data — every file here is reproducible by `python3 cli.py fetch`.
data/
outputs/
# There is no trailing-comment syntax here: `cache/  # why` is a pattern ending in "# why"
# and matches nothing, which is how py3dep's 7.9 MB aiohttp cache nearly shipped.
cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.tif
*.laz
*.npz

# The viewer payload is the one exception: small, downsampled, and committed so the viewer
# works on a fresh clone. Two rules are needed, not one. `data/` above excludes viewer/data as
# a directory, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directory must be un-excluded first. The `**` then reaches the per-site subdirectory: an
# earlier `!viewer/data/*.bin` matched only one level down and silently left dem.bin and the
# whole flood animation untracked, which is a broken viewer on a clone.
!viewer/data/
!viewer/data/**
